# Secrets — never commit credentials
#
# `.env.*` matches `.env.example` too, which is why this audit found the example file
# un-committable: a template with no secrets in it was being ignored by the rule meant to protect
# real ones. The negation below is the fix, and it is deliberately narrow — it re-includes ONLY the
# exact name `.env.example`, so `.env.local`, `.env.production` and every other variant stay ignored.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!_test_keys/**
secrets/
secrets.json

# Client / packaging build artifacts
client/dist/
desktop/dist/
client/src-tauri/target/
desktop/src-tauri/target/
*.dmg
*.msi
*.AppImage
*.deb
*.apk

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Coverage
/coverage/
*.lcov
cobertura.xml

# Foundry dependency, fetched by CI (never committed; see .github/workflows/ci.yml)
contracts/lib/
contracts/cache/
contracts/out/
